{
  "axis": "DX-M1 regime transition curve (compute-bound <-> D2H-bound)",
  "closes": "crossover axis (274bffa) caveat #3: proved 2 regimes exist at the extremes (resnet50 compute-bound / yolo26n D2H-bound) but did not trace the transition",
  "environment": {
    "host": "Raspberry Pi 5 (Cortex-A76 x4, Debian 13)",
    "npu": "DEEPX DX-M1 (3 cores @1000MHz), PCIe Gen2 x1",
    "runtime": "DXRT v3.4.2 (dxbenchmark), FW v2.7.4",
    "method": "fixed heavy conv trunk (body_depth=18, ~2.7ms Inference, all NPU / 0 CPU group) + 4-ch bottleneck + 1x1 expander head sweeps output(D2H) size at constant compute; dxbenchmark synthesizes input (latency/regime only, random weights -> no accuracy claim)",
    "core_map": "-n 1 = 1 core (NPU_0) | -n 4 = 2 cores (NPU_0/1) | -n 0 = 3 cores (NPU_ALL)"
